<title>UK: Allied Domecq shares up, Hoare positive.</title>
<headline>Allied Domecq shares up, Hoare positive.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Allied Domecq Plc firmed 4-1/2 pence to 487, with broker Hoare Govett reiterating its &quot;undervalued&quot; stance.</p>
<p>Analyst Matthew Jordan said he repeated his recommendation following the release earlier this week of positive results from other companies with drinks operations, notably Canada's Seagram Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Jordan also cited favourable conditions in the U.S. spirits market, saying it appears to be growing faster than expected.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
